femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: zip: read exactly the size an entry states, or fail

Every limit on a read (ZipLimits::max_file_read_size, the max_bytes of
read_entry_into_with_limit behind the *_with_limit and *_with_hard_cap
readers, the buffer check of read_file) is checked against the sizes the
central directory states. Nothing held the data to them: a deflated entry
was inflated until its stream ended, so an entry stating 16 bytes could
give megabytes to a writer whose cap was far lower. An archive under 64 KiB
returned 8 MiB through a 2 MiB cap.

1. Both DEFLATE loops (read_file_with_scratch and
   read_file_to_writer_with_scratch; every other read goes through one of
   them) give inflate no output room past the stated size. Inflate may
   still consume the end of the stream there. If it has more to write it
   makes no progress, and the read fails before anything past the stated
   size reaches the buffer or the writer.
2. A stream that ends before the stated size fails too, so that a
   successful read is always exactly the stated size.
3. A stored entry must state the same compressed and uncompressed size.
   Its data was read by the compressed size while the limits and buffers
   were sized by the other.

These fail with the new ZipErrorKind::SizeMismatch (the enum is
non_exhaustive). In read_file_with_scratch a stored entry whose two sizes
differ was BufferTooSmall when the compressed one exceeded the buffer and
is now SizeMismatch.

Upstreamable.

